<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-467] Ace editor focus problem on long contents</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-467</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-437&quot; title=&quot;Autoscroll misbehaving when paragraph status is changing&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-437&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-437&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; includes a fixes on scrolling bug of Ace editor on keyboard navigation for Chrome browser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However in case of ace editor has contents more than window height, the problem still occur.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s because of the fix moves hidden textarea always to 0 offset (relative to code editor), not actual cursor position.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;p&gt;Chrome&lt;/p&gt;</environment>
        <key id="12916446">ZEPPELIN-467</key>
